Here's a possible implementation of the function that returns a valid JSON object:

```javascript
function getPersonData(person) {
  const personData = {
    tags: person.tags,
    id: person.id,
    age: person.age,
    city: person.city
  };

  return personData;
}
```

This function takes a person object as input and returns a JSON object with the keys "tags", "id", "age", and "city".

To use this function, you can call it with a person object as input:

```javascript
const person = {
  tags: ["tag1", "tag2"],
  id: 123,
  age: 25,
  city: "New York"
};

const personData = getPersonData(person);
console.log(personData);
```

This will output:

```json
{
  "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"],
  "id": 123,
  "age": 25,
  "city": "New York"
}

