```javascript
function getAgeAndEmailAndId(data) {
  const age = data.age;
  const email = data.email;
  const id = data.id;

  return {
    age,
    email,
    id
  };
}

// Example usage
const data = {
  age: 25,
  email: "example@email.com",
  id: 123
};

const result = getAgeAndEmailAndId(data);
console.log(result); // { age: 25, email: "example@email.com", id: 123 }
```

In this example, we're using the `getAgeAndEmailAndId` function to extract the age, email, and ID from the `data` object. The function returns a new object with the extracted values.

The `console.log` statement is used to log the extracted values to the console.
